@startuml sdd-04a_order_path
title SDD-04a — One tick becomes one order, HIGH VIEW (UML **sequence diagram**)\nSix messages, one guard. Every call, parameter and alternative is SDD-04b.
autonumber
skinparam maxMessageSize 260

participant "market_data" as MD
participant "strategy" as ST
participant "trading" as TR
participant "binance_gateway" as GW
participant "Binance Futures" as BN <<external>>
participant "surfaces" as UI

MD ->> ST : MarketTickEvent
note right of MD : asynchronous — over the event bus;\nstrategy subscribed in subscribe()
ST -> TR : execute(intent : OrderIntent)
note right of ST : synchronous, typed port call\n(IOrderSubmission)
TR -> GW : create_trading_client()
GW -> BN : POST /fapi/v1/order
BN ->> TR : ORDER_TRADE_UPDATE\n(user-data stream)
TR ->> UI : OrderFilledEvent, PositionChangedEvent
note right of TR : asynchronous — over the event bus,\nthrough trading's feed

note over ST, TR
  **The one guard on this path — the symbol lease.**
  On arm, strategy calls ITradingSession.claim_symbol(symbol, owner_id = "strategy").
  execute() then refuses any intent whose owner_id differs from the lease owner of its
  symbol, with OrderRejectionReason.SYMBOL_LEASED — which is how a manual order from the
  Dev Board on the same symbol is blocked (EPIC-024B §4.1.2's hard block).
end note

note over MD, UI
  **Notice the direction of the synchronous call.** strategy depends on trading, never
  the reverse: trading records a lease for an opaque owner_id and **does not know that
  strategy exists**. That is what keeps the two contexts acyclic (HLD §2.3).
  A surface never waits on the exchange — messages 1 and 6 cross the bus.
end note
@enduml
